Here we use that $S$ is a strictly henselian local ring of characteristic $p$ and hence $S \to S$, $f \mapsto f^ p - f$ is surjective. Also $S$ is a normal domain and hence $\Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U) = S$. Thus $H^1_{\acute{e}tale}(U, \mathbf{Z}/p)$ is the kernel of the map $H^1(U, \mathcal{O}_ U) \to H^1(U, \mathcal{O}_ U)$ induced by $f \mapsto f^ p - f$.